  "question": {
    "text": "An N-P-N transistor is being used in CE mode for which the current transfer ratio is, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">α</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>25</mn><mn>26</mn></mfrac></math>. The input resistance is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1000</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math> and amplitude of A.C. input voltage is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>mV</mi></math>. The amplitude of the amplified output collector current is"
  },
